          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-30 08:49:39.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity test_51f",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity test_51f\n\nsanity test_51f opens and holds 100000 files, closes them and\nunlinks them, in one process. The time is the file count: about\n42s, 20s and 33s for those phases on ldiskfs, and 58s, 27s and\n53s on ZFS DNE, with a mean of 147s over 17556 runs per 30 days\nin CI.\n\n100000 open files on a client is a site requirement, so keep the\ntotal but open them from five processes of 20000 files each at\nthe same time, and unlink them in parallel. Each process uses its\nown directory: in a shared one the MDS serializes the creates and\nunlinks, and five processes were no faster than one. SLOW=yes\nkeeps a single process with 100000 files.\n\nOn a rocky9 ldiskfs cluster of test VMs with separate client, MDS\nand OSS nodes, ONLY=51f took 202s and 209s before and 68s, 64s\nand 73s after; five processes in one directory took 183s and\n167s. If CI scales the same way, that saves about 95s of the 147s\nmean, about 460 hours of CI time per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=51f\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: If1c0c6d07e12bbd3f545dc98e8cd2ae981a9b29e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
